This is the right scientific framing. The object BEAR should model is not “a coin” or even “an influencer.” It is a **latent market regime and information-diffusion process**.

# BEAR META SCIENCE

## 1. What a crypto “meta” actually is

A useful operational definition is:

> A **meta** is a temporary coordination regime in which a coherent narrative causes attention, capital, product activity and social behaviour to become mutually reinforcing across a related group of assets.

That makes it different from simple hype.

A narrative becomes a meta when:

```text
IDEA / CATALYST
      ↓
INFORMED DISCOVERY
      ↓
INDEPENDENT VALIDATION
      ↓
CAPITAL FOLLOWS
      ↓
ATTENTION FOLLOWS
      ↓
PRICE VALIDATES ATTENTION
      ↓
MORE PEOPLE ADOPT THE NARRATIVE
      ↓
MORE CAPITAL ENTERS
      ↓
REFLEXIVE META
```

Eventually:

```text
NOVELTY FALLS
      ↓
EVERYONE KNOWS
      ↓
MARGINAL SOURCE QUALITY FALLS
      ↓
EARLY MONEY DISTRIBUTES
      ↓
MORE ATTENTION PRODUCES LESS PRICE RESPONSE
      ↓
META DECAYS
```

There is actual empirical support for distinguishing **novel information** from mere attention. A recent study using millions of crypto news items finds that greater coverage breadth tends to predict *lower* subsequent returns, while genuinely novel coverage predicts *higher* subsequent returns. Twitter research likewise finds that abnormal investor ticker attention has short-horizon predictive value, while increasing mass attention contributes to herd-like synchronization. ([SSRN][1])

Research on narrative attention additionally finds feedback in both directions: narrative prevalence can precede returns in related cryptocurrencies, while price moves themselves feed narrative prevalence. That's almost precisely the reflexive mechanism we are trying to model. ([ScienceDirect][2])

So:

```text
MENTIONS ↑
```

is **not necessarily bullish**.

Potentially:

```text
NOVEL informed mentions ↑
+
independent sources ↑
+
capital confirmation ↑
```

is bullish.

While:

```text
raw mentions ↑↑↑
novelty ↓
copying ↑
smart-money selling ↑
```

may mean the meta is dying.

