# 2. Model META as a hidden state

I would add this state machine to BEAR:

```text
M0 DORMANT
   No coordinated narrative.

M1 SEED
   Catalyst or novel idea appears.

M2 INFORMED DISCOVERY
   Small/high-quality sources begin noticing it.

M3 INDEPENDENT VALIDATION
   Multiple unrelated informed clusters converge.

M4 REFLEXIVE ACCELERATION
   Attention + capital + price reinforce each other.

M5 AMPLIFICATION
   Major KOLs / mainstream CT arrive.

M6 SATURATION
   Narrative becomes common knowledge.

M7 DISTRIBUTION / DECAY
   Early participants sell; marginal attention stops working.

M8 REVIVAL
   New catalyst creates another wave.
```

Do **not** hardcode that a meme meta lasts three days or an AI meta lasts three months.

Use a **Hidden Semi-Markov Model**, not just an HMM, because duration itself is informative:

```text
P(meta_state_t | everything known ≤ t)
```

with learned state-duration distributions.

Approximate priors might eventually show:

```text
micro-meme burst       hours → days
chain meme meta         days → weeks
sector narrative        weeks → months
macro crypto regime     months
```

but BEAR should discover those distributions.

