# 3. Four scientific models fit together

### HSMM — what state are we in?

Answers:

```text
P(MEME_ACCELERATION) = ?
P(SATURATION) = ?
```

### Hawkes process — how is information spreading?

Crypto narratives are self-exciting.

One event causes more events:

```text
Yeon
 ↓
three trenches accounts
 ↓
Unipcs
 ↓
Ansem
 ↓
20,000 CT accounts
```

A multivariate Hawkes model lets us estimate:

```text
source_i → source_j influence
```

and the reproduction/branching rate of the narrative.

Hawkes-process research is explicitly used for separating endogenous from exogenous event generation and for learning information-diffusion structure. ([DOI.org][3])

### Change-point detection — when did something actually change?

Detect discontinuities in:

```text
attention
wallet flows
DEX volume
holder growth
narrative breadth
cross-asset returns
```

instead of manually declaring:

> meme season started Tuesday.

### Survival analysis — how likely is this meta to die?

Estimate:

```text
hazard(meta ends in next 24h | state)
```

Social presence itself appears relevant to crypto survival: research has found declining/high-quality social attention associated with changes in cryptocurrency failure hazard. ([AIS eLibrary][4])

