# 10. Wallets: yes, use them — but don't make them the brain

Your instinct about X is largely right.

X is unusually useful because it gives us:

```text
WHY
WHAT THESIS
WHAT META
WHEN SOMEONE REALIZED IT
WHAT THEY EXPECT
WHAT WOULD INVALIDATE IT
```

A blockchain cannot tell us that.

Wallets tell us:

```text
WHAT CAPITAL ACTUALLY DID
```

The ideal architecture is therefore:

```text
                  X
        semantic intelligence
                 │
                 ▼
              CLAIM
                 │
        ┌────────┴────────┐
        ▼                 ▼
     MARKET             WALLET
   validation       action validation
        │                 │
        └────────┬────────┘
                 ▼
               GRAPH
```

Wallets should **validate/refute** social intelligence.

